  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the cross-repo trace:\n\n**Babel side** \u2014 `packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts` picks legacy vs stage-3 based on the `legacy`/`version` option and dispatches to `transformer-legacy.ts` (legacy) or `createClassFeaturePlugin` (stage-3, in `babel-helper-create-class-features-plugin/src/index.ts`). Critically, `transformer-legacy.ts` never emits `Reflect.metadata`/`design:paramtypes` calls \u2014 Babel core has no decorator-metadata emitter at all; NestJS DI users on Babel only get metadata via a third-party plugin (`babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`), never from `@babel/plugin-proposal-decorators` itself. `babel-helper-create-class-features-plugin/src/features.ts`'s `shouldTransform` also encodes the well-known ordering gotcha: legacy decorators must be configured *before* `@babel/plugin-transform-class-properties` or Babel throws.\n\n**SWC side** \u2014 `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` wires `.swcrc`'s `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator`/`decoratorMetadata` into `decorators::Config{legacy, emit_metadata}`, built alongside `typescript::Config` in the same pass chain. `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs` dispatches to `legacy::new(emit_metadata)` (and panics `unimplemented!` if you try `emit_metadata` with the non-legacy proposal). `legacy/mod.rs`'s `TscDecorator` runs `ParamMetadata` then, if `metadata` is true, `Metadata::new(...)` **before** children are visited \u2014 and `crates/swc/src/lib.rs`'s doc comment confirms the pipeline guarantee: decorators are handled, then resolver, then TS-node stripping, in that order. So SWC's decorator pass sees live type annotations and can synthesize `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`design:returntype` (`legacy/metadata.rs`, itself a port of `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`'s logic) \u2014 but **only when `decoratorMetadata: true` is set**; it defaults to `false` (`pub decorator_metadata: BoolConfig<false>` in `config/mod.rs`).\n\n**Divergence causing the customer's bug**: the customer's swc config almost certainly has `legacyDecorator: true` (so classes still construct and `@injectable()` fires as a plain call) but omits `decoratorMetadata: true`. Since it defaults false, SWC silently skips emitting `Reflect.metadata` design-type calls, so Nest's `Reflect.getMetadata('design:paramtypes', ...)` reads `undefined` \u2192 the reported crash. Under Babel this same customer must have relied on a separate metadata plugin that never carried over into their swc config \u2014 the fix is adding `\"decoratorMetadata\": true` next to `\"legacyDecorator\": true` in `jsc.transform`.",
